          "description": "Log lines that Loki's `| json` parser rejects. Source labels (code_file_path, code_function_name, code_line_number) tell you which Python file is emitting broken JSON — usually an f-string containing a stray `{` like a dict literal or repr() output. Fix at source by switching the call to structlog kwargs.",
